{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/973516-playing-a-character-with-a-disability","id":973516,"title":"Playing a Character with a Disability","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-20T17:25:06-07:00","id":973516,"title":"Playing a Character with a Disability","content":"How would you stat out a character that's missing the use of their legs or is blind or deaf. How would a werewolf treat another werewolf that has lost a leg. How would being deaf effect a mage ect... I ask because in some games there is a flaw system but i don't see that anywhere in chronicles of darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11277-hyperspacewizard","name":"hyperspacewizard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T17:35:19-07:00","id":973522,"title":"","content":"Most likely with a permanent condition such as leg wrack. Other than that, I think I'll avoid this topic <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T17:39:35-07:00","id":973526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hyperspacewizard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/973516-playing-a-character-with-a-disability#post973516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you stat out a character that's missing the use of their legs or is blind or deaf. How would a werewolf treat another werewolf that has lost a leg. How would being deaf effect a mage ect... I ask because in some games there is a flaw system but i don't see that anywhere in chronicles of darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5439_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5439\" data-vbnamecard=\"5439\">Gullinbursti</a> said. Persistent conditions/tilts. The issue with Uratha is that they <b>will</b> eventually regenerate the lost appendage, barring ST fiat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T17:56:45-07:00","id":973537,"title":"","content":"Yeah, what you're looking for mechanically as the equivalent of &quot;flaws&quot; in other systems is Persistent Conditions and Tilts. On the math level, you take some dice penalty as appropriate, and when the flaw comes up during a session as a hindrance, you take a Beat.<br /> <br /> In terms of roleplaying a character with a disability: ask your group what they're comfortable with. One thing to consider is whether you want the condition to be something that's &quot;fixable&quot; with magic of some sort during play. I can imagine that a blind person might not like the thought that they can only participate fully in this fantastic world if they're &quot;fixed&quot; first, for example, as opposed to imagining their own lived experience with the addition of magic and monsters as a sighted person would. Especially with a long-term disability, the character is probably not going to constantly be saying &quot;woe is me, if only I had my legs, alas, how I miss them.&quot; It's just a fact of life, and one that's modified and worked around with the tools available.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T17:59:16-07:00","id":973539,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that upon coming a werewolf, a person loses all their physical disabilities related to their senses. They grow eyes if they never had them before, they can suddenly hear with perfect clarity, and so forth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T18:47:44-07:00","id":973571,"title":"","content":"Cool does anyone here think that a vampire that was blind would have an advantage over sight focused players when another vampire uses obfuscate I thought that be a neat bonus for a player like tap his shoulder and be like while your buddies are straining their eyes you hear the slick thunk of the wounded prey. I was thinking that a werewolf that was wheel chair bound could really play up the shaman card and maybe turn his wheel chair into some cool spirit fetish. I just like helping my players and some have difficulties you know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11277,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11277-hyperspacewizard","user":"hyperspacewizard","date":". 09-20-2016, 09:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11277-hyperspacewizard","name":"hyperspacewizard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T18:50:04-07:00","id":973573,"title":"","content":"Obfuscate doesn't actually make you invisible, it affects the mind, making you think the one using Obfuscate isn't there. It would, therefore, work against the blind.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T18:52:06-07:00","id":973574,"title":"","content":"If I remember correctly (and I could be wrong, I'm not as solid on Requiem as other settings), but doesn't Obfuscate act more like a mental discipline than one that makes you physically un-seeable. Rather than bending light, it makes you ignore the presence of the obfuscated individual. In that case, I don't think being blind/deaf etc would effect Obfuscation or the obfuscated in any meaningful way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T19:16:55-07:00","id":973585,"title":"","content":"I'm surprised no one has pointed out yet that Blind, Crippled, and Mute are all Persistent Conditions that exist in the core book. A Deaf Condition would probably be a simple matter to write up as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T21:27:15-07:00","id":973641,"title":"","content":"Cool you know thanks for pointing out the conditions I'm still getting used to using them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11277-hyperspacewizard","name":"hyperspacewizard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T22:53:42-07:00","id":973685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hyperspacewizard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/973516-playing-a-character-with-a-disability#post973516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would a werewolf treat another werewolf that has lost a leg.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Ouch. Think you'll get a scar?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Yeah. looking forward to it once the leg grows back. Had it crushed by a truck in a high speed vehicle chase. Pain in the ass to use a wheelchair for two weeks.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Need help covering for the boss?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Nah, I'm good. I'm on vacation.<br /> <br /> <br /> In the older edition, there was I recall something about an NPC werewolf who was a cripple before his first change and that remained despite his transformation. It was possible to lose limbs as well and regenerate them, but it's expensive and costs Willpower dots from what I heard.<br /> <br /> In the current edition, it plays up the regeneration factor much higher and much easier.. To make a long story short, all physical disabilities are temporary conditions as far as the game treats it, just really long lasting temporary conditions. They're still persistent conditions, just... ones that you can remove once you've healed all the damage. Doesn't matter how you got it, if you heal the damage that caused the Tilt, it's restored. Takes a few weeks or months depending on the injury in question though, when you deal with high stamina and high health, the tilts involved tend to require doing a big beating. I know senses get restored mere days after the First change, but I don't recall what the rules are for crippled or lost limbs lost beforehand. I assume they're also covered since you have a rule that says you remove tilts when you have recovered from the damage that caused them.... or there's probably a line of text that clarifies it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 09-21-2016, 01:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T23:20:22-07:00","id":973688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hyperspacewizard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/973516-playing-a-character-with-a-disability?p=973571#post973571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool does anyone here think that a vampire that was blind would have an advantage over sight focused players when another vampire uses obfuscate I</div> </div> </div> </div>No, because it's mind-effecting. But IIRC, Dominate requires eye contact, so that's a hell of an advantage right there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T23:55:26-07:00","id":973697,"title":"","content":"Dominate requires eye contact... but not having eyes also makes it much harder for you to use Dominate as well. Combined with the penalties for being blind in the first place, I'm not sure how big of an advantage that really is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T01:56:28-07:00","id":973724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/973516-playing-a-character-with-a-disability?p=973697#post973697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dominate requires eye contact... but not having eyes also makes it much harder for you to use Dominate as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a really good point, but one has to keep in mind that that usually won't come up unless the player as a blind character chooses to play a Ventrue.<br /> Coming at it from the angle of something that existed from the start of play, anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T06:22:11-07:00","id":973800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hyperspacewizard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/973516-playing-a-character-with-a-disability#post973516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would a werewolf treat another werewolf that has lost a leg.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/973516-playing-a-character-with-a-disability?p=973685#post973685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Ouch. Think you'll get a scar?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Yeah. looking forward to it once the leg grows back. Had it crushed by a truck in a high speed vehicle chase. Pain in the ass to use a wheelchair for two weeks.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Need help covering for the boss?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Nah, I'm good. I'm on vacation.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Golden! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/973516-playing-a-character-with-a-disability?p=973685#post973685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In the current edition, it plays up the regeneration factor much higher and much easier.. To make a long story short, all physical disabilities are temporary conditions as far as the game treats it, just really long lasting temporary conditions. They're still persistent conditions, just... ones that you can remove once you've healed all the damage. Doesn't matter how you got it, if you heal the damage that caused the Tilt, it's restored. Takes a few weeks or months depending on the injury in question though, when you deal with high stamina and high health, the tilts involved tend to require doing a big beating.</div> </div> </div> </div>I made fan <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/484426-yours-2ed-conditions#post484426\">Scar Persistent Conditions for 2E Werewolves</a> that mark your wounds lasting from previous battle. Could aplay them when you end the source Condition of wound.<br /> <br /> <b>Scar (Persistant)</b><br /> It is honorable thing to get scar from memorable hunt in Uratha culture and most werewolves take pride in leaving marks of the previous battles on they flesh, even if they bodies wants to heal them. This character made sure her previous fatal wound, lost organ or ripped off limb healed only enough to show that it was lost. Character can leave Scar on herself after getting the Tilt in battle that would left major wounds, like Blindness, Arm or Leg Wrack. She writes name of original Tilt and enemy that was source of it. So werewolf that lost one eye in fight with Pure writes this Condition as <b>Scar (One Eye - Pure)</b> on character sheet.<br /> <b>Effect:</b> Character takes half of modifiers from normal Tilt (rounded down) all the time from half cured effect. When faced with enemy that made her the Scar, character get's +1 bonus to all action against this particular prey, fueled by the memories of her hunt that left he Scar on her.<br /> <b>Resolution: </b>Character spend Willpower dot and let her regeneration abilities to heal her scar.<br /> <b>Beat: </b>Character encounters a limitation or difficulty that inconveniences her, streaming from the Scar. Your character speaks or listen to the story of how she got her Scar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-21-2016, 09:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T06:46:35-07:00","id":973822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/973516-playing-a-character-with-a-disability?p=973800#post973800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Scar (Persistant)</b><br /> It is honorable thing to get scar from memorable hunt in Uratha culture and most werewolves take pride in leaving marks of the previous battles on they flesh, even if they bodies wants to heal them. This character made sure her previous fatal wound, lost organ or ripped off limb healed only enough to show that it was lost. Character can leave Scar on herself after getting the Tilt in battle that would left major wounds, like Blindness, Arm or Leg Wrack. She writes name of original Tilt and enemy that was source of it. So werewolf that lost one eye in fight with Pure writes this Condition as <b>Scar (One Eye - Pure)</b> on character sheet.<br /> <b>Effect:</b> Character takes half of modifiers from normal Tilt (rounded down) all the time from half cured effect. When faced with enemy that made her the Scar, character get's +1 bonus to all action against this particular prey, fueled by the memories of her hunt that left he Scar on her.<br /> <b>Resolution: </b>Character spend Willpower dot and let her regeneration abilities to heal her scar.<br /> <b>Beat: </b>Character encounters a limitation or difficulty that inconveniences her, streaming from the Scar. Your character speaks or listen to the story of how she got her Scar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does the bonus additionally override the usual penalties? IE, if I had a tilt that put me at -4 for something, and I scar it, the penalty reduces to -2, right?<br /> <br /> If I then fight my favored prey, am I at +1(Penalty Voided, +1 Bonus), or -1 (-2 penalty, +1 bonus)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T07:24:36-07:00","id":973837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/973516-playing-a-character-with-a-disability?p=973822#post973822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the bonus additionally override the usual penalties? IE, if I had a tilt that put me at -4 for something, and I scar it, the penalty reduces to -2, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, half the Tilt modifier.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/973516-playing-a-character-with-a-disability?p=973822#post973822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If I then fight my favored prey, am I at +1(Penalty Voided, +1 Bonus), or -1 (-2 penalty, +1 bonus)</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on what you are doing. Bonus +1 is to all actiona with the Scar's prey. Tilt penalties works like original Tilt, only halved. So if you would have penalty from Tilt to particular action, you now get half of this penalty. If action is on Scar's prey, you also get bonus +1 on those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":